WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:01.037
(coin dropping)

00:00:01.037 --> 00:00:05.204
(Pac-Man video game music playing)

00:00:08.265 --> 00:00:09.098
- [Voiceover] I'm Billy Mitchell,

00:00:09.098 --> 00:00:10.980
video game player of the century.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.282
I did the world's first
perfect score on Pac-Man.

00:00:14.282 --> 00:00:15.115
3,333,360.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:20.884
Ooh, it's exhausting to just say it.

00:00:20.884 --> 00:00:23.380
I began in the competitive
world of pinball.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.312
It moved to Donkey Kong.

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:27.022
But the greatest level of competition

00:00:27.022 --> 00:00:29.167
at the moment was Pac-Man.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.233
(Pac-Man video game sound effects)

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:33.299
If I was gonna be the best,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.545
if I had to be the best at the game

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:35.881
that was everywhere.

00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:38.427
So in 1999, I sent out a press release.

00:00:38.427 --> 00:00:39.789
I was as cocky as could be.

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:41.452
They said, "There's been
ten billion games played,

00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:42.470
"How are you gonna do it?"

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.945
I said, "'Cause I'm Billy Mitchell."

00:00:43.945 --> 00:00:46.752
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:48.352
You start off on the first board,

00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:50.233
but on board 21, that's where it reaches

00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.995
maximum difficulty.

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:53.436
You have to navigate all the way

00:00:53.436 --> 00:00:57.676
to board 255 doing the
same repetitive thing.

00:00:57.676 --> 00:00:59.791
You can't miss a dot, a prize,

00:00:59.791 --> 00:01:00.897
a blue man.

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:02.756
You can't die once.

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:03.609
You can't lose focus.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:05.439
You gotta stay with it all the way there.

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:07.396
Four-to-five hours.

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:08.915
You have to take a corner,

00:01:08.915 --> 00:01:11.940
down to 160th of a
second in order to create

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.300
perfect timing.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.739
And keep your eye right here.

00:01:14.739 --> 00:01:16.128
Right here.

00:01:16.128 --> 00:01:18.877
(Pac-Man video game sound effects)

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:22.033
You have to do that over 29,000 times

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:25.219
without making any mistakes and dying.

00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:27.290
You play 255 boards.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.164
On 256, there's enough memory left

00:01:29.164 --> 00:01:31.015
in the game for the
left half of the board,

00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:33.417
and not the right half.

00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:35.567
The right half is filled
with computer garble.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.798
Anything and everything
that is not Pac-Man.

00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:39.885
Different walls, different dots.

00:01:39.885 --> 00:01:42.327
That's what a perfect score is.

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:45.241
The moment that score went up there,

00:01:45.241 --> 00:01:48.375
I thought, "Wow, I achieved perfection."

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:49.208
You get to the end.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.369
There's nothing to do but die.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:52.061
There was nothing saying,
"Congratulations.”

00:01:52.061 --> 00:01:54.278
There was nothing saying,
"The End, Game Over.”

00:01:54.278 --> 00:01:55.418
Nothin'.

00:01:55.418 --> 00:01:58.450
The designer of Pac-Man,
not only did he never think

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.362
anyone would get to the end,

00:02:00.362 --> 00:02:02.288
he didn't know where the end was.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.461
He didn't know at what point the game

00:02:03.461 --> 00:02:04.565
would run out of memory.

00:02:04.565 --> 00:02:06.854
Everything to him is completely baffling.

00:02:06.854 --> 00:02:08.693
They never saw the split screen

00:02:08.693 --> 00:02:10.946
until I sent it to them.

00:02:10.946 --> 00:02:12.656
Masaya Nakamura, who's the Godfather

00:02:12.656 --> 00:02:15.238
of video games, he crowned me

00:02:15.238 --> 00:02:16.676
"Video Game Player of the Century"

00:02:16.676 --> 00:02:20.636
for that and all the
previous achievements.

00:02:20.636 --> 00:02:23.077
It doesn't get any higher than that.

00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:26.744
(upbeat instrumental music)

